-*   **Codeword Assignment Strategy:** Not specified in sources. Huffman coding is explicitly mentioned as a common implementation [S1][S2].
-*   **Combination with RLE:** Fixed-length Huffman coders are sometimes combined with RLE to accelerate decoding [S1][S2].
+*   **Codeword Assignment Strategy:** Huffman coding or arithmetic coding [S1][S2][S4, unofficial].
+*   **Combination with RLE:** Fixed-length Huffman coders are sometimes combined with RLE to accelerate decoding [S2][S3].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Random Access:** Variable-length encoding makes it difficult to quickly reconstruct an arbitrary sequence of data, which is critical in massively parallel GPU settings [S1][S2].
-*   **Decoding Complexity:** Entropy encoding implies significantly more computational work during decoding compared to fixed-length schemes [S1][S2].
+*   **Random Access:** Variable-length encoding makes it difficult to quickly reconstruct an arbitrary sequence of data, which is critical in massively parallel GPU settings [S2][S3].
