 ### Golomb-Rice Encoding
-An entropy encoder favored over arithmetic and Huffman coding in some volume rendering contexts because it offers better random access capabilities and lower computational complexity [S1][S2]. It is particularly useful when fast random access for reconstruction is required [S2].
+An entropy encoder favored over arithmetic and Huffman coding in some volume rendering contexts because it offers better random access capabilities and lower computational complexity [S2][S3]. It is used when fast random access for reconstruction is required [S2].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Decoding requires significantly more computational work than fixed-length encoding [S1][S2].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Decoding requires significantly more computational work than fixed-length encoding [S2][S3].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
 *   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
 *   **Scaling:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **Strengths:** High compression ratio due to exploitation of data distribution [S1][S2].
-*   **Limitations:** Variable-length nature hinders quick random access reconstruction, which is critical in massively parallel GPU settings [S1][S2]. Implies more work during decoding [S1][S2].
-*   **When to use:** When high compression ratios are needed for on-disk storage and decoding can be performed before rendering time, or when combined with RLE to accelerate decoding [S1][S2].
-*   **When not to use:** When fast random access is required directly on the GPU during rendering, in which case Golomb-Rice or fixed-length schemes may be preferred [S1][S2].
