 ## Background
-Entropy encoding has been widely used in compressed volume rendering since early applications [S2]. Huffman encoding and arithmetic encoding are frequently used, often combined with RLE [S1][S2]. Research has focused on finding encoding schemes with fast random access for reconstruction, such as Golomb-Rice encoding, to address the limitations of traditional entropy encoders in parallel settings [S1][S2]. A survey by Komma et al. benchmarks and analyzes lossless compression encodings for compressed volume data, including entropy encodings [S1][S2].
